#' Generate the local weighting strategy for all intersection hypotheses
#'
#' @description
#' Computes the closure-based weighting strategy for a graphical multiple
#' testing procedure: for each of the \eqn{2^m - 1} intersection
#' hypotheses. Returns a combined matrix of intersection
#' membership indicators and hypothesis weights.
#'
#' @param w `NumericVector` (length m) of initial local hypothesis weights.
#' @param G `NumericMatrix` (m x m) initial transition matrix.
#' @returns `NumericMatrix` (\eqn{2^m - 1} x \eqn{2m}). The first m columns
#'   are 0/1 intersection-membership indicators; the second m columns are
#'   the corresponding local hypothesis weights (0 where the hypothesis
#'   is not in that intersection).
#'
#' @note
#' This function implements Algorithm 1 of Bretz et al. (2011). The output
#' follows the convention established in
#' `gMCP::generateWeights()` and
#' `graphicalMCP::graph_generate_weights()`.
#'
#' @references
#' Bretz, F., Maurer, W., Brannath, W., and Posch, M. (2009). A graphical
#' approach to sequentially rejective multiple test procedures.
#' Statistics in Medicine, 28(4), 586--604.
#' <https://doi.org/10.1002/sim.3495>
#'
#' Bretz, F., Posch, M., Glimm, E., Klinglmueller, F., Maurer, W., and
#' Rohmeyer, K. (2011). Graphical approaches for multiple comparison
#' procedures using weighted Bonferroni, Simes, or parametric tests.
#' Biometrical Journal, 53(6), 894--913.
#' <https://doi.org/10.1002/bimj.201000239>
#'
#' @noRd
calc_local_weights <- function(w, G) {
    .Call(`_multigrain_calc_local_weights`, w, G)
}

